From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 05:14:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: apple,s8000-display-pipe: Add the
 display DART windows
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The A9 display pipe reads memory through dart-disp0, which iBoot leaves
in bypass. The DART cannot get a node of its own: binding apple-dart to
it would reset the streams under the live scanout. The display driver
only needs to read its translation control registers to confirm that
the scanout bypasses translation before it takes the display over.

Add the two dart-disp0 windows (Apple device tree order: 0x206304000,
then 0x206300000) as optional "dart0" and "dart1" reg entries, and name
all reg entries so the optional ones can be found by name.

This is part of J71t ledger 11.1.

Reported-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml     | 27 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml
index b6a297a91..7626d7f8f 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml
@@ -14,14 +14,17 @@ description:
   with the compatible "adbe0,s8000" in the Apple device tree. It contains
   the ADP/ADBE display pipe that scans out to the internal eDP panel. The
   bootloader leaves the pipe, the eDP link and the panel running; the pipe
-  reads memory through the display DART, which the bootloader leaves in
-  bypass.
+  reads memory through the display DART (dart-disp0), which the bootloader
+  leaves in bypass. The DART has no node of its own: it must not be reset
+  under the running scanout, so its two register windows are listed here
+  and only read, to check that the scanout bypasses translation.
 
 properties:
   compatible:
     const: apple,s8000-display-pipe
 
   reg:
+    minItems: 6
     items:
       - description:
           ADP window, with the control and interrupt registers, the
@@ -31,6 +34,20 @@ properties:
       - description: Display block window C
       - description: Display block window D
       - description: Seven-register side block
+      - description: Display DART (dart-disp0), first window
+      - description: Display DART (dart-disp0), second window
+
+  reg-names:
+    minItems: 6
+    items:
+      - const: adp
+      - const: disp-a
+      - const: disp-b
+      - const: disp-c
+      - const: disp-d
+      - const: side
+      - const: dart0
+      - const: dart1
 
   interrupts:
     items:
@@ -71,7 +88,11 @@ examples:
                   <0x2 0x06440000 0x0 0x8000>,
                   <0x2 0x06480000 0x0 0x8000>,
                   <0x2 0x064c0000 0x0 0x8000>,
-                  <0x2 0x06500000 0x0 0x1c>;
+                  <0x2 0x06500000 0x0 0x1c>,
+                  <0x2 0x06304000 0x0 0x4000>,
+                  <0x2 0x06300000 0x0 0x4000>;
+            reg-names = "adp", "disp-a", "disp-b", "disp-c", "disp-d",
+                        "side", "dart0", "dart1";
             interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
             interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 140 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
                          <AIC_IRQ 143 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
